# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile copies exactly four things: requirements.txt, caper/,
# run-manage-py.sh and gunicorn_config.py. Everything listed here sits outside
# all four, so excluding it cannot change what ends up in the image -- it only
# stops the daemon reading megabytes it will never use, and in one case stops
# the build failing outright.
#
# That one case is neo4j/. The neo4j container bind-mounts a directory inside
# this checkout and writes conf/ as uid 7474 mode 700, so `docker build .` on
# the dev server died on `checking context: can't stat neo4j/conf` before it
# ran a single instruction. Nothing in the image has ever come from there.

neo4j/

# Not copied, and the largest things in the tree: .git is the whole history and
# test_data is ~130 MB of tarballs the test suite reads from the working
# directory, never from the image.
.git/
test_data/

# Runtime state that only exists on a deployed checkout.
tmp/
logs/
backups/
prod-writes/

# Local scratch. `holding/` is an old copy of three application modules sitting
# untracked on the dev server; nothing imports it.
holding/
.claude/

# Python and editor droppings.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
